inophen 15 mg/kg PO/IV for fever and comfort.\n\n**Vaccination status & counseling**\n- Note incomplete Hib immunization; Hib remains a leading pathogen in unvaccinated children. Document the gap and arrange for catch‑up Hib vaccination once the acute illness resolves.\n- Discuss the importance of age‑appropriate immunizations with the parents.\n\n**Infection‑control precautions**\n- Implement droplet precautions (surgical mask, eye protection, gown, gloves) for all staff until the causative organism is identified and appropriate isolation can be discontinued.\n- Use a private room (ideally negative‑pressure if available) for the airway procedure.\n\n**Monitoring & disposition**\n- Admit to the pediatric ICU for continuous pulse‑oximetry, cardiac monitoring, and frequent airway reassessment.\n- Repeat lateral neck X‑ray or bedside ultrasound only if clinically indicated.\n- Communicate clearly with the family about the emergent nature of the airway, the steps being taken, and the plan for ongoing care.\n\nThis plan addresses airway protection, empiric therapy, adjunctive steroids, the relevance of the child’s vaccination history, and necessary infection‑control measures.",
